ary color in the RGB color model and a secondary color in the CMYK color model, and is the complementary color of cyan. Reds range from the brilliant yellow-tinged scarlet and vermillion to bluish-red crimson, and vary in shade from the pale red pink to the dark red burgundy."}],"image":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/c/cf/Delicious_fresh_strawberries_%284735910403%29.jpg/330px-Delicious_fresh_strawberries_%284735910403%29.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Red"}],"images":[{"srcset":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/c/c1/Scrooges_third_visitor-John_Leech%2C1843.jpg/500px-Scrooges_third_visitor-John_Leech%2C1843.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 1x, https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/c/c1/Scrooges_third_visitor-John_Leech%2C1843.jpg/1280px-Scrooges_third_visitor-John_Leech%2C1843.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 2x","src":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/c/c1/Scrooges_third_visitor-John_Leech%2C1843.jpg/500px-Scrooges_third_visitor-John_Leech%2C1843.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail","alt":"The Ghost of Christmas Present as illustrated by John Leech for Charles Dickens's A Christmas Carol (1843)","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/File%3AScrooges_third_visitor-John_Leech%2C1843.jpg"},{"srcset":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/1/17/08_St._Nikolaas_bij_een_Snoeper.png/330px-08_St._Nikolaas_bij_een_Snoeper.png?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 1x","src":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/1/17/08_St._Nikolaas_bij_een_Snoeper.png/330px-08_St._Nikolaas_bij_een_Snoeper.png?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail","alt":"1850 illustration of Saint Nicholas and his servant Père Fouettard/Zwarte Piet","